<!-- Statement of Earnings and Deductions: a typewriter-set statement in IBM Plex Mono,
     with italic section headings, two outlined identity boxes, a rule-bracketed ledger
     and a fully gridded summary.

     Type is deliberately uneven, as in the reference: the company block reads large, the
     ledger is set several sizes down, and the summary sits between them. Monospace is wide
     - roughly 0.6em per character - so column widths here are sized from character counts
     ("FICA - Social Security" is 22 characters), not from eyeballed proportions.

     Optional lines (salary vs hourly, overtime, bonus, state paid leave) are their own
     renderIf tables repeating the same fixed widths, since renderIf drops a table but
     cannot drop a row. The wage-type branch tests isSalaried / isHourly, because renderIf
     tests one path and both wageType strings are truthy.

     Sized for the printable page: 720 x 960 CSS px. See CLAUDE.md, one stub one sheet. -->
